## Install the package

<InstallationTabs pkg="svelte-pdf-mini" />

`svelte-pdf-mini` targets **Svelte 5.57+** (runes, attachments) and the latest evergreen browsers. It depends on `pdfjs-dist` 6, `runed`, `svelte-toolbelt` and `@floating-ui/dom`. `@cantoo/pdf-lib` (PDF export) and KaTeX / marked (Markdown notes) are loaded lazily on first use. See [Bundlers & deployment](/docs/deployment) for exact requirements, non-Vite bundlers, CORS and CSP.

## Import the styles (optional)

```ts
import 'svelte-pdf-mini/styles.css';
```

The stylesheet holds the pdf.js text-layer rules, focus effects and calm defaults for the floating UI (menus, popovers, cards, side notes, tables of contents). Every value is a CSS variable; skip it entirely if you style the parts yourself.

## Worker and assets

pdf.js runs in a Web Worker. With Vite the worker is set up automatically and **shared by every document** on the page. Character maps, standard fonts and the WASM decoders load from jsDelivr by default; to self-host them, call `configurePdf` once, before the first document loads:

```ts
import { configurePdf } from 'svelte-pdf-mini';

configurePdf({
	cMapUrl: '/pdfjs/cmaps/',
	standardFontDataUrl: '/pdfjs/standard_fonts/',
	wasmUrl: '/pdfjs/wasm/'
});
```

Copy the folders from `node_modules/pdfjs-dist/` into your `static/` directory. `configurePdf` also accepts `workerSrc`, `workerPort` (a ready `Worker` to use instead), `documentOptions` (merged into every `getDocument()` call), `sharedWorker: false` and `bitmapCacheBytes` (memory for off-screen page bitmaps, default 192 MB).

<Callout title="Server-side rendering">
	Components render their static shell on the server and only start loading documents in the browser, after hydration. No special setup is needed in SvelteKit, and prerendering works. See <a href="/docs/deployment#ssr-and-prerendering">SSR and prerendering</a>.
</Callout>
